+## BIOS CHECK
+
+`GAME SETTINGS > BIOS SETTINGS > BIOS CHECK` (the row is also offered at
+`GuiMenu.cpp:2832` where the BIOS script is supported), mapped by T31 S8
+(#678, #1234; D-UI-039): the fork-modified `GuiBios` page. While the check
+runs, `PLEASE WAIT`. Then one list: a row per system, its name and its
+summary sentence (`ALL PRESENT (N)`, or how many are missing and how many
+are not a known version). On a row, the help bar offers DETAILS (south),
+which opens the system's own page, titled by its name, a file per row:
+`PRESENT`, `MISSING`, or `PRESENT, BUT NOT A KNOWN VERSION`. BACK closes
+the page; START is REFRESH, which runs the check again. When the check
+returns nothing, the list is one sentence: `THE BIOS CHECK RETURNED
+NOTHING`, or, once T21's `a73ed9efc` and this lane's S6 are integrated,
+`COULDN'T CHECK THE BIOS FILES RIGHT NOW.` with its next step on the page
+(#1244). S6 (#1245, #1246) makes the summary one sentence per count and
+DETAILS a row's prompt only.
+
+## SCRAPING GAMES
+
+`SCRAPER > SCRAPE NOW` closes SCRAPER and opens SCRAPING GAMES (`GuiScraperRun`,
+the fork's page), mapped by T31 S8 (#678, #1234): a fourth-tier page with
+CANCEL (D-UI-078). Under its title, seven lines: the status (`PREPARING...`,
+`SCRAPING...`, then the outcome), the counter (`GAME N OF M`), the game
+being scraped, its detail, a note, `ELAPSED` with the time, and the footer
+(`THIS CAN TAKE A WHILE.`, then `PRESS ANY BUTTON TO CLOSE`). While it runs,
+the back button is CANCEL: `CANCEL SCRAPING?` / `WHAT'S SCRAPED SO FAR IS
+KEPT. UPDATE GAMELISTS TO APPLY IT.` with YES and NO. The outcome is one of
+three words (D-UI-028): `COMPLETED`; `SKIPPED - YOU CANCELLED IT` for the
+player's cancel (D-UI-129, the word kept); or `COULDN'T FINISH` when the
+scraper refused the run or some games could not be scraped. The counts line
+(`GAMES SCRAPED: N  ·  COULDN'T SCRAPE: M`) and the next step (`UPDATE
+GAMELISTS TO APPLY CHANGES.`) follow. This lane's S7 (#1247) adds the why
+and the next step for a run with failures, and makes a button dismiss the
+page only once its outcome has been drawn.
+
